## Decisions made (and why)
- Fixed-column, moving-table architecture over gantry: shorter
  force loop, ~3-5× stiffness needed for steel vs aluminum
- Epoxy granite fill for damping: mass is the cheapest rigidity,
  and gravel is free
- Bought rails/screws instead of scavenging: printer rods can't
  hold tolerance under steel cutting loads — this is the precision
  floor of the machine

